[CENTER]
[SIZE=7][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Leaf[/COLOR][COLOR=#2C3E50]RTP[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4][B][COLOR=#7F8C8D]Free Random Teleport (RTP) Plugin for Paper, Spigot, Fabric & NeoForge[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[/CENTER]

[CENTER][I]Once upon a time, I wanted to explore a minecraft world. I asked for [/I]/rtp[I] in servers I played on. They told me "no, that's laggy", and I took that personally.[/I][/CENTER]

No menu, however polished, can make [I]/rtp[/I] fast - only the engine behind it can. With most random-teleport plugins, [B]any[/B] click can make the server load chunk after chunk after chunk: it picks a spot, loads it on the main thread, and - if it turns out unsafe - tries another, and another, with nothing telling it to stop. That lag spike never shows up in the menu. It shows up in your MSPT, in the stutter every other player feels, and eventually in the players who quietly stop logging in.

[B]LeafRTP was built on one idea: a teleport should cost the server nothing the player can feel. No spike. No spinner. No quiet churn.[/B]

[B]Benchmarked, not asserted.[/B] 19.8 TP/s sustained at a 4 ms worst-case main-thread tick on Paper (next-best plugin: 70 ms), with audited safety invariants - no unsafe blocks, no force-loaded chunks, no claim-bypassing teleports, no silent failures. Every number on this page is measured on a public harness you can rerun yourself.

[CENTER]
[I]Supported: Paper, Spigot, Fabric, and native NeoForge (1.21.x / 26.1.x) - Minecraft 1.20.x / 1.21.x / 26.x. Legacy Forge is not native: run this jar under Arclight / Mohist. Send your players to a safe, random spot, engineered to maintain 20.0 TPS without lag spikes.[/I]

[SIZE=4][COLOR=#27AE60][B]100% Free.[/B][/COLOR] Same engine as the paid [URL='https://builtbybit.com/resources/rtp-pro.105418'][B]LeafRTP-Pro[/B][/URL] build. No paywalled [I]/rtp[/I] or nag screens, and no ads - just anonymous [URL='https://bstats.org/']bStats[/URL] usage stats (server-admin opt-out via [I]plugins/bStats/config.yml[/I]). Core engine and lite binary are [B]MIT-licensed[/B] - open source, forkable, commercially usable.[/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B][COLOR=#16A085]Trusted since 2021: 4.6 stars over 30+ reviews, 430k+ downloads.[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B]Latest builds, Folia-tagged releases, and beta channels also live on [URL='https://modrinth.com/plugin/leafrtp']Modrinth[/URL][/B] - auto-updater and Pterodactyl friendly.[/SIZE]

[/CENTER]
[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]Why operators pick LeafRTP[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[CENTER][SIZE=5][B][COLOR=#27AE60]19.8 TP/s sustained at 4 ms worst-case tick. Next-best plugin: 70 ms.[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE][/CENTER]

[B]If [I]/rtp[/I] is the top entry in your timings report, this is the fix.[/B] LeafRTP is the fastest free Random Teleport plugin for Bukkit-native Minecraft servers (Paper, Bukkit, Arclight, Mohist, and other Bukkit-family forks), with Fabric supported as a first-class platform:

[LIST]
[*][B]No lag spikes when players spam [I]/rtp[/I].[/B] Worst-case main-thread tick stays at 4 ms (vs. 70-852 ms for the next plugins) - your TPS holds at 20.00 during a teleport burst.
[*][B]Instant teleports, no "Finding a safe location..." wait.[/B] Pre-verified location queue serves [I]/rtp[/I] in one tick instead of loading chunks on demand.
[*][B]Works on plain Bukkit servers at Paper-class speed.[/B] Off-tick [I].mca[/I] Anvil pre-filter, worst tick stays at 3 ms while competitors spike past 3 seconds.
[*][B]Runs on Folia[/B] out of the box - regionized scheduling + async teleport, no extra config.
[*][B]Cross-server [I]/rtp[/I] without Redis or SQL[/B] - the [I]proxy-direct[/I] transport lets a Velocity lobby send players to a backend region over a lightweight TCP socket, no database required.
[*][B]Clickable [I]/rtp menu[/I] GUI world & region selection[/B] - players pick worlds and regions from an interactive book menu (Paper / Folia; chat-paginated elsewhere), no commands to memorize.
[*][B]Eight claim-plugin integrations bundled[/B] (GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, Lands, WorldGuard, Towny, Factions, HuskTowns, RedProtect) - no add-ons to install.
[*][B]Per-player cooldowns & usage limits[/B] - per-permission cooldown and limit nodes out of the box, so /rtp spam is capped without an extra plugin.
[*][B]Configurable arrival title, sound & effects[/B] - the on-screen teleport title/subtitle, sounds, and particle/firework effects are all tunable per region, so the landing looks and feels like your server.
[*][B]Audited safety[/B]: no unsafe blocks, no force-loaded chunks, no claim-bypassing teleports, no silent failures.
[/LIST]

On [B]Paper 1.21[/B], measured on the in-repo benchmark harness, two clients spamming [I]/rtp[/I] back-to-back:

