[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#27AE60]See the engine work: real-time visual diagnostics[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
Most random-teleport plugins are a black box - you find out a region is full of unsafe ground only when players start complaining. LeafRTP turns that into something you can [I]watch[/I].

Run [I]/rtp scan[/I] on a region and hold the map: LeafRTP paints each sector green (safe) or red (unsafe) [B]as it verifies it[/B], live, on a real vanilla map item - while the chat readout streams [I]cps[/I], land %, and an [B]ETA[/B] so you know exactly how long a pre-warm will take.

[CENTER][URL='https://youtu.be/Ftjy1zw_S04'][B]Watch the scan paint a region live (video)[/B][/URL][/CENTER]

[LIST]
[*][B]Two passes, and the heavy one runs off-tick.[/B] The first pass reads [I].mca[/I] Anvil region files on a background pool - it never touches the main thread (S-005) and throws out most of a region (ocean, wrong biome, obviously unsafe) before any chunk is loaded. Only the survivors reach the second pass, a throttled live chunk-load verification; because the Anvil pre-filter has already discarded the bulk of the region, that live pass is a small fraction of what a naive pre-generator would load, and it is paced so a scan can run on a live server without tanking TPS.
[*][B]It is a diagnostic, not a chore.[/B] The red/green map and the rejection breakdown in [I]/rtp info[/I] tell you [I]why[/I] a region rejects coordinates (bad biome, unsafe block, claim), so you can tune [I]safety.yml[/I] against evidence instead of guesswork.
[*][B]Free, and cross-platform.[/B] The held-map heatmap ships in the free build on Paper, Spigot, Fabric, and NeoForge - not a static PNG you export to disk and open over FTP.
[/LIST]

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#2980B9]Runtime observability built in (/rtp info)[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
No metrics add-on, no external dashboard. [I]/rtp info[/I] reports the numbers an operator actually watches, sampled without blocking a tick:

[LIST]
[*][B]TPS (1m / 5m / 15m) and live server MSPT[/B] with tick-budget utilisation.
[*][B]JVM heap[/B] used / max, and current chunk-ticket leak rate.
[*][B]Pipeline latency percentiles[/B] (P50 / P75 / P90 / P95 / P99) and slow-teleport count.
[*][B]Generation success / failure rate[/B] with the top coordinate-rejection cause and a full breakdown by cause.
[*][B]Queue depth and growth warnings[/B], plus database round-trip latency.
[/LIST]

This is the part competitors describe as "enterprise-grade" in their listing copy. Here it is a command you can run, with every field traced to a requirement in [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/dev/TRACEABILITY.md'][B]TRACEABILITY.md[/B][/URL].

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#C0392B]Requirements[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
A few hard requirements. If any are a [B]no[/B], EssentialsX [I]/rtp[/I] or HuskHomes are fine free alternatives.

[LIST]
[*]✅ [B]Java 21+[/B] on your host (REQ-RTP-SYS-001, non-negotiable).
[*]✅ [B]Paper, Spigot, or a Bukkit-family fork[/B] (Arclight / Mohist supported for Forge bridges). Fabric and NeoForge (1.21.x / 26.1.x) are supported and regularly tested, at feature parity with the Bukkit family in the latest builds.
[*]✅ [B]In-game editing or YAML, your call.[/B] Browse and tune config from the clickable [I]/rtp menu[/I] (book on Paper / Folia, chat-paginated elsewhere), or edit the plain YAML files directly and version-control them.
[*]✅ [B]Runs on Folia[/B] out of the box - regionized scheduling + async teleport, no extra config. The tuned, throughput-optimized Folia adapter ships first in [B]LeafRTP-Pro[/B].
[*]✅ [B]Vault economy[/B] works in the free build - charge players per [I]/rtp[/I] with per-region price, biome surcharges, and a balance floor; cost refunded automatically on cancel or pipeline failure; dormant when Vault is not installed.
[*]✅ [B]Cross-server [I]/rtp[/I] without Redis or SQL[/B] - the [I]proxy-direct[/I] transport (Velocity) ships in the free build. SQL/Redis shared-state backends ship in [B]LeafRTP-Pro[/B].
[/LIST]

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#16A085]Install (30 seconds)[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Drop [I]LeafRTP-x.y.z.jar[/I] into [I]plugins/[/I].
[*]Start the server. A [I]default[/I] region is generated for you.
[*]Type [B]/rtp[/B].
[*]Run [B]/rtp menu[/B] to browse regions, worlds, and configuration in-game (clickable book on Paper / Folia, chat-paginated fallback elsewhere).
[/LIST]

Tune [I]plugins/RTP/config.yml[/I] and [I]plugins/RTP/regions/*.yml[/I] later - via [I]/rtp menu[/I] or by editing the YAML directly. Full admin guide is auto-unpacked into [I]plugins/RTP/docs/[/I] on first run, and lives online at the [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/FOR_SERVER_ADMINS.md'][B]admin guide[/B][/URL].

[CENTER][COLOR=#A0A0A0]------------------------------------------------------------[/COLOR][/CENTER]

[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#2980B9]Core capabilities[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]🌀 [B]Deterministic spiral selection[/B] — bounded math, no unbounded re-roll loops. Predictable on huge worlds.
[*]🧠 [B]Spatial memory that persists across restarts[/B] — LeafRTP [I]learns[/I] which sectors keep failing and stops trying them.
[*]⏱️ Most [I]/rtp[/I] calls serve instantly from a [B]pre-generated location queue[/B] — destinations are chunk-loaded and verified before you type the command.
[*]🛡️ [B]Safety pipeline[/B] — radius check, invulnerability timer, optional landing platform, movement / damage cancel timers, material allow/deny list.
[*][B]Optional PvP / combat-tag gate[/B] - off by default; when enabled, /rtp is refused or delayed for players who recently dealt or took PvP damage, so a teleport can't be used to escape a fight. Native combat tracking, with optional PvPManager / CombatLogX / Simple Combat Log integration.
[*]🏛️ [B]Per-region arrival schematics[/B] — drop a [I].schem[/I] named after a region into [I]plugins/RTP/schematics/[/I] and every teleport into that region pastes it (a lobby pad, arrival shrine, or custom platform) on the landing spot. Cross-platform Sponge [I].schem[/I], decoded in-house (no WorldEdit required), claim-aware and audited.
[*]🌍 [B]Per-region, per-world config[/B] — shapes (square / circle / rectangle), curve weighting, vertical adjustors, sky-light check, world overrides, hot-reloadable YAML.
[*]✨ [B]Effects on every lifecycle phase[/B] — particles, sounds, fireworks, potion, note effects via the in-tree [I]effects-api[/I], gated by [I]rtp.effects.<name>[/I] permissions.
[*]🔗 [B]Eight claim-plugin integrations bundled[/B] — GriefDefender, GriefPrevention, Lands, WorldGuard, Towny, Factions, HuskTowns, RedProtect.
[*]🧩 Iris, Terra, and custom datapack generators work out of the box, with modded biome IDs preserved. [B]PlaceholderAPI[/B] and [B]ProtocolLib[/B] are supported as optional soft-deps.
[*]💰 [B]Optional Vault economy[/B] - charge players per [I]/rtp[/I] with per-region price, [I]priceOther[/I], params/biome surcharges, and a balance floor ([I]economy.yml[/I]); cost refunded automatically on cancel or pipeline failure ([I]refundOnCancel: true[/I] default); dormant when Vault is not installed.
[*]🛠️ [B]Public [I]rtp-api[/I][/B] - same surface as Pro. Trigger LeafRTP from a GUI, NPC, or quest; build your own UX without forking.
[*]🗺️ [B]Live map / heatmap visualizations[/B] - [I]/rtp scan[/I] paints region safety state (green safe / red unsafe) onto a real held map item while the chat readout streams cps, land %, and ETA. Free on Paper, Spigot, Fabric, and NeoForge.
[*]📊 [B]Built-in runtime observability[/B] - [I]/rtp info[/I] reports TPS/MSPT (spark-enhanced when spark is installed), JVM heap, pipeline latency percentiles, generation success/failure breakdown, and a [I]/rtp info biomes[/I] player-occupancy leaderboard - no metrics add-on needed.
[*]🌐 [B]12 locales, parity-enforced[/B] - shipped locales are CI-verified so a translated server never silently falls back to English on a new key.
[*]📚 [B]Unusually thorough engineering docs[/B] - 28+ dated ADRs and a requirements-to-tests trace, public: [URL='https://github.com/dailystruggle/RTP/blob/V3/docs/dev/INDEX.md'][B]docs/dev/INDEX.md[/B][/URL].
[/LIST]

